---
import FieldGuideLayout from '../../../components/FieldGuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<FieldGuideLayout
  title="Sprite runtime pipeline"
  description="From an overlay's sprite-place call to OAM hardware. Shadow-OAM in BSS, VBlank DMA flush, sprite-slot manager."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: 'How the Game Works', href: `${base}/field-guide/how-the-game-works/` },
    { label: 'Sprite pipeline' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    Companion to <a href={`${base}/field-guide/2d-art/composition-recipes/`}>2D Art › Composition</a>.
    This page traces a single sprite placement from the overlay code that
    requested it through the engine's bookkeeping into NDS hardware OAM.
  </p>

  <h2>Stage 1 — overlay places a sprite</h2>
  <p>
    A controller / body overlay calls the engine sprite API in
    <code>ov137</code>:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`FUN_021850D4(
    slot,          // sprite-slot index (allocated earlier via FUN_02184990/FUN_021849AC)
    x, y,          // screen coords
    w, h,          // pixel dimensions
    type,          // 1=BG, 2=OBJ, 4=blend, …
    flags,         // priority, layer, blend mode
    data_ptr       // pointer into the content-cache (NCGR + NCLR bytes)
);`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>FUN_021850D4</code> calls <code>func_0x02071E78</code> (arm9-side
    sprite emitter). 12 distinct ov137 functions call this entry point.
  </p>

  <h2>Stage 2 — engine bookkeeping (ov137 internal)</h2>
  <p>Engine API table:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_02184990(?, n_tiles)</code></td><td>Allocate sprite slot.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_021849AC(?, n_tiles, flag)</code></td><td>Allocate sprite slot with flag.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_02185508(size, align)</code></td><td>malloc for sprite-related structs.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_0218472C(slot, mask, val, flag)</code></td><td>Attribute set.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_021848A8(slot, mask, val)</code></td><td>Attribute set.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_02184814(slot, mask, val, flag)</code></td><td>Attribute set variant.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_02185154(slot, ?, ?, ?, ?)</code></td><td>Sprite position update.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_02185384(?, ?, ?, ?)</code></td><td>Write attribute.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_021852A8(?, ?, ?)</code></td><td>Tile-data update.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>FUN_02184D6C(?, ?, ?, ?, &local, ?)</code></td><td>Sprite-list builder.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Stage 3 — write to shadow OAM</h2>
  <p>
    ov137 writes 8 bytes of OAM data per sprite to a <strong>shadow OAM</strong>
    buffer in main RAM (BSS). Sprite-slot address computed by the chain:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`oam_slot_addr = *0x021907BC + i * 0x40 + field_offset

  *0x021907BC  → base of sprite-slot array (28 writes observed)
   i * 0x40     → 64 bytes per slot record
   field_offset → 0x00..0x07 holds OAM attr0/attr1/attr2`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Stage 4 — VBlank DMA flush</h2>
  <p>
    At VBlank, the engine DMAs the shadow buffer to hardware OAM. Two VBlank
    handlers cooperate:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Handler</th><th>Address</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>arm9</td><td><code>0x0207001C</code></td><td>System-side VBlank (audio, DMA timing)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ov137</td><td><code>0x02185BF8</code></td><td>Game-engine VBlank (DMAs shadow OAM/VRAM)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Transfer wrappers</h2>
  <p>
    Each wrapper takes <code>(src, dst_off, byte_count)</code> and dispatches
    to the DMA0 primitive <code>FUN_02017D9C</code> at
    <code>0x040000B0..0x040000BC</code> (DMA0 source / dest / count /
    control).
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Wrapper</th><th>Destination</th><th>Hardware base</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x020769C0</code></td><td>OAM main</td><td><code>0x07000000 + dst_off</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x02076A00</code></td><td>OAM sub</td><td><code>0x07000400 + dst_off</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x02076A40</code></td><td>OBJ VRAM main</td><td><code>0x06400000 + dst_off</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x02076A7C</code></td><td>OBJ VRAM sub</td><td><code>0x06600000 + dst_off</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>OAM manager pointers (BSS)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Address</th><th>Refs</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x020A749C</code></td><td>42</td><td>ARM9 OAM manager pointer</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x02190908</code></td><td>—</td><td>ov137 OAM manager pointer</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x021907BC</code></td><td>28 writes</td><td>ov137 sprite-slot array pointer</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x021A55C0</code></td><td>750</td><td>Game state struct pointer (top-most BSS reference)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Dispatcher (ov137)</h2>
  <p>
    <code>FUN_021708CC</code>: command dispatcher with a 10-entry jump table
    at <code>0x021708E6</code>. Each opcode handler sits at offset
    <code>(table[op] + 0x021708E8)</code>. Called 98 times across overlays.
  </p>

  <h2>Pipeline summary</h2>
  <pre><code>{`controller overlay (e.g. ov003)
       │  loads asset via FUN_02009894 → master cache table 0x020AA740
       ▼
body overlay (e.g. ov070) walks placement table at .rodata
       │  for each entry: FUN_021850D4(slot, x, y, w, h, type, flags, data)
       ▼
ov137 sprite API
       │  STR/STRH into shadow-OAM at *0x021907BC + i*0x40 + offset
       ▼
[VBlank fires]
       │
       ▼
ov137 VBlank handler @ 0x02185BF8
       │  calls 0x020769C0  (OAM main transfer wrapper)
       │  → FUN_02017D9C  (DMA0 primitive)
       │    → 0x040000B0..BC (DMA registers)
       ▼
NDS hardware OAM @ 0x07000000
       │
       ▼
GPU rasterises sprites at scanline time`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>notes/phaseA_ghidra/DISCOVERIES.md</code> §"OAM/sprite rendering pipeline"</li>
    <li><code>arm9_full_plaintext.bin</code> @ <code>0x02017D9C</code> — DMA primitive</li>
    <li><code>ov137</code> — engine VBlank + sprite API</li>
  </ul>
</FieldGuideLayout>
